# Modus Modal Implementation Guide

## 🎯 Overview

This rule documents the correct implementation patterns for Modus Web Component modals in React/Next.js applications, including critical solutions for common issues.

## 🚨 Critical Issue: Modal Methods Not Available

### ❌ The Problem

When using `ModusWcModal` in React, you cannot call `showModal()` and `close()` methods directly on the component reference:

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - These methods don't exist on the Modus component
const modalRef = useRef<HTMLModusWcModalElement>(null);

const openModal = () => {
  modalRef.current?.showModal(); // ❌ Error: showModal is not a function
};

const closeModal = () => {
  modalRef.current?.close(); // ❌ Error: close is not a function
};
```

### 🔍 Root Cause

**Modus Web Components wrap native HTML elements**: The `ModusWcModal` component wraps a native `<dialog>` element internally, but doesn't expose the dialog methods directly on the component interface.

### ✅ The Solution: Access Inner Dialog Element

**Use `querySelector('dialog')` to access the native dialog element:**

```tsx
"use client";

import { ModusWcModal } from "@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-react";
import { ReactNode, useRef, useEffect } from "react";

interface ModusModalProps {
  modalId: string;
  isOpen?: boolean;
  onClose?: () => void;
  children: ReactNode;
  // ... other props
}

export default function ModusModal({
  modalId,
  isOpen = false,
  onClose,
  children,
  ...otherProps
}: ModusModalProps) {
  const modalRef = useRef<HTMLModusWcModalElement>(null);

  // ✅ CORRECT - Control modal visibility
  useEffect(() => {
    const modal = modalRef.current;
    if (modal) {
      if (isOpen) {
        // Find the inner dialog element and call showModal
        const dialogElement = modal.querySelector("dialog");
        if (dialogElement) {
          dialogElement.showModal();
        }
      } else {
        // Find the inner dialog element and call close
        const dialogElement = modal.querySelector("dialog");
        if (dialogElement) {
          dialogElement.close();
        }
      }
    }
  }, [isOpen]);

  // ✅ CORRECT - Handle modal events
  useEffect(() => {
    const modal = modalRef.current;
    if (modal) {
      const handleClose = () => {
        onClose?.();
      };

      // Listen for modal close events on the inner dialog
      const dialogElement = modal.querySelector("dialog");
      if (dialogElement) {
        dialogElement.addEventListener("close", handleClose);

        return () => {
          dialogElement.removeEventListener("close", handleClose);
        };
      }
    }
  }, [onClose]);

  return (
    <ModusWcModal ref={modalRef} modal-id={modalId} {...otherProps}>
      {children}
    </ModusWcModal>
  );
}
```

## 🎯 Key Implementation Patterns

### 1. Modal State Management

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Use React state to control modal
const [isModalOpen, setIsModalOpen] = useState(false);

<ModusModal
  modalId="myModal"
  isOpen={isModalOpen}
  onClose={() => setIsModalOpen(false)}
>
  Modal content
</ModusModal>;
```

### 2. Event Handling

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Listen to native dialog events
useEffect(() => {
  const modal = modalRef.current;
  if (modal) {
    const dialogElement = modal.querySelector("dialog");
    if (dialogElement) {
      const handleClose = () => onClose?.();
      dialogElement.addEventListener("close", handleClose);

      return () => {
        dialogElement.removeEventListener("close", handleClose);
      };
    }
  }
}, [onClose]);
```

### 3. Modal Attributes

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Use all available modal attributes
<ModusWcModal
  modal-id="uniqueId"           // Required: Unique identifier
  backdrop="static"             // "default" | "static"
  position="center"             // "top" | "center" | "bottom"
  fullscreen={false}            // boolean
  show-fullscreen-toggle={true} // boolean
  show-close={true}             // boolean
  custom-class="my-modal-class" // string for custom styling
  aria-label="Modal description" // Accessibility
>
```

### 4. Slot-Based Content

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Use slots for structured content
<ModusWcModal modal-id="structuredModal">
  <div slot="header">
    <div className="text-xl font-semibold">Modal Title</div>
  </div>
  <div slot="content">
    <div className="text-base">Modal body content</div>
  </div>
  <div slot="footer">
    <ModusWcButton color="secondary" onButtonClick={closeModal}>
      Close
    </ModusWcButton>
  </div>
</ModusWcModal>
```

## 🚫 Common Anti-Patterns

### ❌ Don't Try Direct Method Calls

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - These will fail
modalRef.current?.showModal();
modalRef.current?.close();
modalRef.current?.open = true;
```

### ❌ Don't Use Incorrect Event Listeners

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - Events won't fire on the component itself
modalRef.current?.addEventListener("close", handleClose);
```

### ❌ Don't Forget Cleanup

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - Memory leaks without cleanup
useEffect(() => {
  dialogElement.addEventListener("close", handleClose);
  // Missing cleanup function
}, []);
```

## 🔧 Debugging Tips

### 1. Check Inner Dialog Exists

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  const modal = modalRef.current;
  if (modal) {
    const dialogElement = modal.querySelector("dialog");
    console.log("Dialog element found:", !!dialogElement);
  }
}, []);
```

### 2. Verify Event Listeners

```tsx
const handleClose = () => {
  console.log("Modal closing"); // Debug log
  onClose?.();
};
```

### 3. Check Modal ID Uniqueness

```tsx
// ✅ Ensure each modal has a unique ID
<ModusModal modalId="modal-1" />
<ModusModal modalId="modal-2" />
```

## 📋 Implementation Checklist

- [ ] ✅ **Use `querySelector("dialog")`** to access native dialog element
- [ ] ✅ **Call methods on inner dialog** not the Modus component
- [ ] ✅ **Add event listeners to inner dialog** for close events
- [ ] ✅ **Include cleanup functions** in useEffect
- [ ] ✅ **Use unique modal IDs** for each modal instance
- [ ] ✅ **Control state via React** not direct DOM manipulation
- [ ] ✅ **Use slot-based content** for structured modals
- [ ] ✅ **Test all modal attributes** (backdrop, position, fullscreen)

## 🎯 Why This Works

1. **Native Dialog Foundation**: Modus modals are built on HTML `<dialog>` elements
2. **Component Wrapping**: The Modus component wraps but doesn't expose dialog methods
3. **DOM Access**: `querySelector` gives us access to the inner native element
4. **Standard Methods**: Native dialog has `showModal()` and `close()` methods
5. **Event Bubbling**: Dialog events bubble up and can be captured

## 🚀 Performance Considerations

### Efficient Modal Management

```tsx
// ✅ Use useCallback for stable references
const handleClose = useCallback(() => {
  setIsModalOpen(false);
}, []);

// ✅ Memoize modal content if expensive
const modalContent = useMemo(() => <ExpensiveComponent data={data} />, [data]);
```

## 🔗 Related Patterns

This pattern applies to other Modus components that wrap native elements:

- **Dialogs**: Use `querySelector("dialog")`
- **Forms**: Access inner form elements
- **Custom Elements**: Query for wrapped native elements

---

**Remember**: Always access the inner native element when you need to call methods or add event listeners that aren't exposed by the Modus Web Component wrapper.
